WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.708
The module challenge asks you to build one
analytical query for a

00:00:03.721 --> 00:00:09.526
decision-maker The question is which sales
categories generated meaningful

00:00:09.553 --> 00:00:15.496
revenue and how much each qualifying category
contributed Start by defining

00:00:15.522 --> 00:00:20.262
one output row as one category Then choose at least
two useful

00:00:20.275 --> 00:00:25.973
aggregate measures The challenge also requires a
row-level condition in WHERE

00:00:25.987 --> 00:00:30.200
and a group-level condition in HAVING Make sure you
can explain why

00:00:30.226 --> 00:00:35.829
each condition belongs where you placed it Finally
sort the result so

00:00:35.842 --> 00:00:41.412
the most important categories are easy to see Do not
focus only

00:00:41.438 --> 00:00:46.336
on producing SQL that runs Write two short sentences
explaining what the

00:00:46.349 --> 00:00:49.573
result means and how the row filter differs from the
group filter

00:00:50.507 --> 00:00:53.441
That explanation is part of the analytical work
